From 3e9b5b511caa6159f744ee87ff84b5b498bc8bcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:28:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 73/76] doc/examples/transcode: stop with an error when
 decoding fails

If avcodec_send_packet() fails, the read loop is left with "break". The
code after the loop then flushes the decoders, filters and encoders,
writes the trailer and returns 0. A damaged input therefore produces a
silently truncated output and the example reports success:

  $ doc/examples/transcode damaged.aac out.m4a
  Decoding failed
  $ echo $?
  0

Jump to the cleanup code instead, like the other error paths in the
loop do, so that the error code is kept. The example now prints
"Error occurred: Invalid data found when processing input" and returns
1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/transcode.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/examples/transcode.c b/doc/examples/transcode.c
index d735fae..d0ccbf3 100644
--- a/doc/examples/transcode.c
+++ b/doc/examples/transcode.c
@@ -599,7 +599,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
             ret = avcodec_send_packet(stream->dec_ctx, packet);
             if (ret < 0) {
                 av_log(NULL, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Decoding failed\n");
-                break;
+                goto end;
             }
 
             while (ret >= 0) {
